==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|vika|vīka}}, from {{inh|sv|non|[[víkja]], [[víkva]]}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*wīkwaną}}.

The adverb in the phrase ''ge vika'' comes from Low German ''wike gewen'', where the noun ''wike'' means ''eftergift, flykt''.<ref>{{R:runeberg.org|saol|6|0303.html Vika}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Sv-vika.ogg|audio|lang=sv}}

===Adverb===
{{head|sv|adverb}}

# (in the expression: ''[[ge]] vika'') to [[give in]], to [[fold]] (under pressure), to give up

===Verb===
{{head|sv|verb}}

# to [[fold]]
# {{lb|sv|colloquial}} to [[dedicate]] (time), to [[designate]] a period of time for a certain action
#: ''Jag '''viker''' en dag åt mässan.''
#:: I dedicate a day to (visiting) the expo.
# {{lb|sv|colloquial}} to dedicate, to set aside for a special person or a special use
#: ''De här kakorna har jag '''vikt''' åt stackars Tom - rör dem inte!''
#:: These cookies I have put aside for poor Tom - don't touch them!
# {{lb|sv|reflexive}} to [[give up]], to [[give in]] (under pressure)
#: ''Mona Sahlin '''viker''' sig inte i första taget.''
#:: Mona Sahlin doesn't give up easily.
# {{lb|sv|reflexive}} to bend (by laughing too much)
#: ''De skrattade så att de '''vek''' sig.''
#:: they were rolling on the floor laughing.
# {{lb|sv|reflexive}} to [[sleep]], to go to bed
#: ''Jag går och '''viker''' mig.''
#:: I'm going to bed.
; vika [[ut]]
# {{lb|sv|transitive}} to [[unfold]], to open a [[foldout]]
# {{lb|sv|reflexive}} to expose oneself as a (nude) [[centerfold]], to appear (nude) in a magazine or online
#: ''Ungdomar '''viker ut''' sig som aldrig förr.''
#:: Youngsters expose themselves like never before.

